<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<model version="NetLogo 7.0.3" snapToGrid="false">
  <code><![CDATA[breed [citizens citizen]
breed [police officer]

globals [agent-vision]

citizens-own [hardship grievance risk-aversion perceived-arrest-risk active? release-tick]
turtles-own [moved-this-tick?]

to setup
  check-jail-term
  clear-all
  set agent-vision vision_in_patches

  let citizen-count round (0.7 * count patches)
  ask n-of citizen-count patches [
    sprout-citizens 1 [
      set hardship random-float 1
      set risk-aversion random-float 1
      set grievance hardship * (1 - legitimacy)
      set active? false
      set color blue
    ]
  ]
  let police-count round (0.04 * count patches)
  ask n-of police-count patches with [not any? turtles-here] [
    sprout-police 1 
  ]
  update-all-agents
  update-police-colors
  reset-ticks
end

to go
  if not any? turtles [ stop ]
  check-jail-term
  ask citizens with [hidden? and release-tick <= ticks] [ release-citizen ]
  ask turtles with [not hidden?] [
    if not hidden? [
      move-randomly
      ifelse breed = citizens
        [ update-citizen-state ]
        [ arrest-active-citizen ]
    ]
  ]
  tick
end

to update-citizen-state  ; citizen procedure
  set grievance hardship * (1 - legitimacy)
  let officers-seen count police in-radius agent-vision
  let active-nearby 1 + count ((other citizens in-radius agent-vision) with [active?])
  set perceived-arrest-risk 1 - exp (- risk-sensitivity * floor (officers-seen / active-nearby))
  set active? (grievance - risk-aversion * perceived-arrest-risk) > activation-threshold
  set color ifelse-value active? [red] [blue]
end

to move-randomly
  let destinations (patches in-radius agent-vision) with [not any? turtles-here with [not hidden?]]
  set moved-this-tick? any? destinations
  if moved-this-tick? [ move-to one-of destinations ]
end



to update-all-agents
  ask turtles [
    set moved-this-tick? false
  ]
  
end

to update-police-colors
  ask police [set color yellow]
  
end


to-report percent-active
  if not any? citizens [ report 0 ]
  report 100 * count citizens with [active?] / count citizens
end

to arrest-active-citizen  ; officer procedure
  let suspect one-of (citizens in-radius agent-vision) with [active? and not hidden?]
  if suspect != nobody [
    ask suspect [
      set active? false
      set color blue
      set release-tick ticks + 1 + random maximum-jail-term
      hide-turtle
    ]
  ]
end

to release-citizen  ; citizen procedure
  if any? other turtles-here with [not hidden?] [
    move-to one-of patches with [not any? turtles-here with [not hidden?]]
  ]
  show-turtle
end

to check-jail-term
  if maximum-jail-term < 1 or maximum-jail-term != floor maximum-jail-term [
    error "Enter a positive whole number for maximum-jail-term."
  ]
end]]></code>
  <widgets>
    <view x="220" wrappingAllowedX="true" y="10" frameRate="30.0" minPycor="0" height="404" showTickCounter="true" patchSize="10.0" fontSize="10" wrappingAllowedY="true" width="404" tickCounterLabel="ticks" maxPycor="39" updateMode="1" maxPxcor="39" minPxcor="0"></view>
    <button x="15" y="20" height="40" disableUntilTicks="false" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="95" display="Setup">setup</button>
    <button x="15" y="72" height="40" disableUntilTicks="false" forever="true" kind="Observer" width="95" display="Go">go</button>
    <input x="13" multiline="false" y="129" height="60" variable="vision_in_patches" type="number" width="192">2.0</input>
    <input x="13" multiline="false" y="203" height="60" variable="legitimacy" type="number" width="192">0.82</input>
    <input x="13" multiline="false" y="273" height="60" variable="activation-threshold" type="number" width="192">0.1</input>
    <monitor x="220" precision="1" y="430" height="61" fontSize="11" width="150" display="% active">percent-active</monitor>
    <input x="13" multiline="false" y="343" height="60" variable="risk-sensitivity" type="number" width="192">2.3</input>
    <input x="13" multiline="false" y="413" height="60" variable="maximum-jail-term" type="number" width="192">30.0</input>
    <plot x="220" autoPlotX="true" yMax="1120.0" autoPlotY="false" yAxis="Citizens" y="504" xMin="0.0" height="200" legend="true" xMax="25.0" yMin="0.0" width="404" xAxis="Tick" display="Citizen states">
      <setup></setup>
      <update></update>
      <pen interval="1.0" mode="0" display="Quiet" color="-13345367" legend="true">
        <setup></setup>
        <update>plotxy ticks count citizens with [not active? and not hidden?]</update>
      </pen>
      <pen interval="1.0" mode="0" display="Active" color="-2674135" legend="true">
        <setup></setup>
        <update>plotxy ticks count citizens with [active?]</update>
      </pen>
      <pen interval="1.0" mode="0" display="Jailed" color="-7500403" legend="true">
        <setup></setup>
        <update>plotxy ticks count citizens with [hidden?]</update>
      </pen>
    </plot>
  </widgets>
  <info><![CDATA[## O_m4 · Rebellion, arrest, and release

## What changes from O_m3

At the start of each tick, citizens due for release return to the grid. Then all officers and free citizens take turns in random order. Each tries to move, then performs the action for their role. They still act if no vacant patch is within reach.

Citizens call `update-citizen-state` after trying to move. They estimate arrest risk using the rounded-down local ratio of police to active citizens. A citizen becomes active when grievance minus net risk exceeds the activation threshold (`G - R * P > T`).

Officers call `arrest-active-citizen` after trying to move. If an officer sees any active citizens within vision, they choose one at random to arrest. The officer stays on their current patch. The arrested citizen becomes quiet and is hidden from the grid.

NetLogo’s built-in `hidden?` flag represents detention in this model. `hide-turtle` sets it to `true` at arrest, and `show-turtle` clears it at release. The model checks the flag when each agent’s turn comes. A citizen arrested earlier in the same tick skips their turn. Other agents can use a jailed citizen’s patch.

Each jail term is drawn uniformly from 1 through **maximum-jail-term**, which defaults to 30 ticks. A released citizen returns to their former patch if it is vacant, or to a randomly chosen vacant patch. They keep their original hardship and risk aversion.

## What to look for

The **Citizen states** plot counts quiet citizens who are free, active citizens, and jailed citizens. Hold the numeric inputs fixed and compare the activity with O_m3. In Epstein’s Model I, an outburst begins when the active count rises above 50 and ends when it falls below 50.

Use Epstein’s Table 2 for published run settings. This course model uses the rounded-down risk rule from the older NetLogo implementation.]]></info>
